# Samba username map (see "username map" in smb.conf): <unix user> = <SMB login names>
# "frog" is the shared, well-known login for Windows (which won't do guest access): it logs in as pi, with
# pi's Samba password (sudo smbpasswd -a pi). The only share is read-only, so it can only ever read.
pi = frog
